I dont' see the *init-hook* functions being called.

I have this in ~/.boclrc, and the "Have fun!" doesn't occur.

    (in-package "CL-USER")
    (use-package "BOCL")

    (format t "~2%Welcome to ~A~2%"
            (lisp-implementation-type)
            (lisp-implementation-version))

    (push (lambda ()
            (format t "~&Have fun!~%")
            (finish-output))
          bocl:*init-hook*)

    (push (lambda (signum)
            (format t "~%Oops got signal ~A!~%" signum)
            (finish-output))
          bocl:*abort-hook*)


    (push (lambda (status)
            (format t "~%Bye, bye, cruel world! (with status ~A)~%" status)
            (finish-output))
          bocl:*quit-hook*)


- the ~/.boclrc init file is not loaded.

- the documentation doesn't mention the init files, the can be one of:

| # | Stem                                | Bare allowed? |
|---+-------------------------------------+---------------|
| 1 | ~~/.bocl{,rc}{,.lisp,.fasl}~        | yes           |
| 2 | ~~/.config/bocl/init{.lisp,.fasl}~  | no            |

The first one that matches is loaded (.fasl is loaded if more recent than .lisp).

So the order tried is:

| .bocl                  |
| .bocl.fasl             |
| .bocl.lisp             |
| .boclrc                |
| .boclrc.fasl           |
| .boclrc.lisp           |
| .config/bocl/init.fasl |
| .config/bocl/init.lisp |

After the first file amongst these is found and loaded (if no -n -norc
--no-init option is given), all the -i | --init options are processed
and the specified init files are loaded.

After this, *init-hook* are called.

Then we enter the REPL.
  
