;; ===================== RESOLUTION (Slices 59 + 60) =====================
;; All items fixed:
;; - ~/.boclrc now loaded: rc search order is ~/.bocl{,.fasl,.lisp},
;;   ~/.boclrc{,.fasl,.lisp}, ~/.config/bocl/init.{fasl,lisp}; first match wins,
;;   .fasl defers to a newer .lisp sibling.  (main.c)  [Slice 59]
;; - *INIT-HOOK* / *QUIT-HOOK* now fire (they were never reached because the rc
;;   file that registered them was not loaded).  [Slice 59]
;; - *ABORT-HOOK* now fires on termination signals too (SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP),
;;   not just SEGV/BUS/ABRT; crash handler installed unconditionally with a
;;   re-entrancy guard.  (kernel.c)  [Slice 59]
;;   (Underlying enabler: fixed HANDLER-CASE non-local pass-through FATAL, which
;;    also broke BOCL:QUIT through the appease loader.  [Slice 59])
;; - ~ in namestrings now abbreviates (USER-HOMEDIR-PATHNAME): (PATHNAME "~/x")
;;   => $HOME/x; added USER-HOMEDIR-PATHNAME.  (kernel.c physical_pathname,
;;   prelude)  [Slice 60]
;; - Unhandled-condition report now applies the format arguments (was printing
;;   the raw format-control, e.g. literal ~S): kernel_ERROR renders the report
;;   via PRINC (princ_to_string).  [Slice 60]
;; - Init files + search order documented (documentation.org, Extensions > The
